 stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 7:30 PM EST Thursday was 12.4 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to fall below flood stage late\ntonight and continue falling to 6.7 feet Tuesday evening.\n- Flood stage is 11.0 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 11.3\nfeet on 03/29/1970.\n- https://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nMotorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued Friday morning at 1100 AM EST.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSTBW"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS82 KTBW 130054"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING NOW IN EFFECT UNTIL FRIDAY MORNING"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.EXT.KTBW.FL.W.0015.000000T0000Z-261113T1600Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-11-13T11:00:00-05:00"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1d98b97646141930e0974afa81b1fc4ab4be0094.001.1,2026-11-11T20:05:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ab9463c844640ac31b5ba411a025321971a1af45.001.1,2026-11-11T12:19:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7ba53d3c2ed8735248fe37e223222c41f28255a3.001.1,2026-11-11T08:20:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.fd02ed8d4416613ada171cea96e88e0cafa64a88.001.1,2026-11-10T19:56:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.737eded5ea347eb1643ca23fab5d4ff26989de60.001.1,2026-11-10T07:32:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a8d93b165cad30aa34fd7683a8d721661ad489bf.001.1,2026-11-09T20:13:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.43278f43ba0cd86ab2150be7c135c5ae5f19e2ad.001.1,2026-11-09T08:29:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.403508bd92a225be8cc937a7943b181aa50a9a91.001.1,202