nole County.\n\n.Heavy rainfall has caused river levels on the St. Johns near Geneva\nAbove Lake Harney to reach Moderate flood stage. River levels may\nfluctuate slightly, but are forecast to generally remain around 9.1\nfeet through the weekend and into next week.\n\nFor the St. Johns River...Above Lake Harney...Moderate flooding is\nforecast.\n\n* WHAT...Moderate flooding is occurring and forecast.\n\n* WHERE...St Johns River near Above Lake Harney.\n\n* WHEN...Until further notice.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 9.0 feet, Water enters the first story of homes on\nWhitcomb Drive between Crossover Lane and Lake Harney Road. Water\ncovers Mullet Lake Park.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 7:30 PM EST Thursday the stage was 9.1 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 6.0 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 7:30 PM EST Thursday was 9.1 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to remain nearly steady around\n9.1 through the weekend and into next week.\n- Flood stage is 8.0 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Motorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued Friday afternoon at noon EST.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSMLB"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS82 KMLB 130139"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL FURTHER NOTICE"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.KMLB.FL.W.0007.000000T0000Z-000000T0000Z/"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.74c745e794d1d8e559a07c71e20e072593439e0f.001.1,2026-11-11T20:45:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1090a929c84ca5c60e1fa1e2c1f9abd629f2547d.001.1,2026-11-11T08:39:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e4cb99847a805aeb5278526ed5fadc4317dba317.001.1,2026-11