ine":"Flood Warning issued November 12 at 11:41AM MST until November 17 at 11:00AM MST by NWS Phoenix AZ","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by upstream dam release continues.\n\n* WHERE...Maricopa County in south central Arizona...\nNortheastern Yuma County in southwestern Arizona...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1100 AM MST Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is expected. Low-water crossings are\nlikely to become inundated with water and may not be passable.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1140 AM MST, water releases from Painted Rock Dam continue\nwith flow peaking at 3000 cfs.\n- Flooding is expected along the Gila River.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nFarmlands and low-water crossings along the Gila River.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSPSR"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS85 KPSR 121841"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING FOR THE UPSTREAM RELEASE OF PAINTED ROCK DAM ON THE GILA RIVER REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL 11 AM MST TUESDAY"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.KPSR.FA.W.0044.000000T0000Z-261117T1800Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-11-17T11:00:00-07:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["FLS"],"NationalWeatherService":["FAW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.eed05b6b397d90a7d16c832f95d8be75f742ff8b.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-81.23,28.7],[-81.39,28.9],[-81.31,28.93],[-81.17,28.79],[-81.23,28.7]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.eed05b6b397d90a7d16c832f95d8be75f742ff8b.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oi